# Project Kit: keep the phone launcher byte-verbatim (its line endings are original)
"REMOTE START/Remote-Start.ps1" -text
"REMOTE START/Remote-Start.bat" -text
# Project Kit: append-only logs - on conflicting appends, keep BOTH sides
"PROJECT KNOWLEDGE/06-DECISIONS-LOG.md" merge=union
"PROJECT KNOWLEDGE/07-CHANGELOG.md" merge=union
"PROJECT KNOWLEDGE/08-MISTAKES.md" merge=union
# KB1 (spec S3-1): the extractor writes LF and its --check compares raw bytes, so a CRLF checkout (core.autocrlf true on
# this PC) would read four identical files as "differs". Committed on its own BEFORE the merge, so the merge writes LF.
ai_player/knowledge/seasoned/*.json text eol=lf
